  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a crowd of men, one prominently in the foreground with an intense, grieving expression, raising their fists in what appears to be a moment of collective anguish or protest. The overlaid text reads: 'when god grants you a child after 20 years of your marriage and israel bombs him few years later.' This juxtaposition of a deeply personal tragedy — the loss of a child — with the geopolitical context of Israeli bombing is intended to evoke strong emotional responses. The meme uses the image of collective grief to frame the narrative of Palestinian suffering, particularly in the context of the Israeli-Palestinian conflict. While not explicitly targeting a specific protected group with slurs or stereotypes, the meme is harmful because it leverages a universally understood human tragedy to amplify political grievances, potentially inciting anger or reinforcing divisive narratives. It is not abusive or cyberbullying in the direct sense, but it is propagandistic in nature, aiming to influence viewers' perceptions of the conflict by associating Israeli military action with the loss of innocent lives, thereby potentially justifying or intensifying anti-Israel sentiment. The intent is to evoke empathy for Palestinian victims while implicitly blaming Israel for the tragedy, using the visual of collective mourning to amplify the message.",
